The [[☃ definition 2]] will pass through points $(2,g(2))$ and $(3,g(3))$.

$\begin{align}
\text{slope}&=\dfrac{\text{change in }y}{\text{change in }x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{g(3)-g(2)}{3-2}
\end{align}$

![Function g is graphed. The x-axis goes from negative 1 to 4. The graph consists of a curve. The curve moves upward through quadrant 3 and (0, 0) to about (1, 0.5), moves downward through (2, g of 2) and (3, g of 3), and ends in quadrant 1. A secant line connects the 2 points.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/a4ea4cd5f0d8309c1a6fae6837ea9189a25b31dc)

We will need to know the values of $g(2)$ and $g(3)$ to find the slope.

$\begin{align}
g(2)&=\dfrac{2}{2^2+1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2}{5}
\\\\
g(3)&=\dfrac{3}{3^2+1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{3}{10}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the slope:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{g(3)-g(2)}{3-2}&=\dfrac{\dfrac{3}{10}-\dfrac{2}{5}}{1}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{1}{10}
\end{align}$
